llot."]}, "overview": "Michigan's governor's race is an open-seat contest between Democrat Jocelyn Benson and Republican John James, with Gretchen Whitmer term-limited. Polling across more than two dozen surveys puts Benson ahead by roughly seven points, with recent live-interview polls from YouGov, Siena and Marist showing leads between three and twelve points. Betting markets price her chances above ninety percent, and most race raters call the contest Lean D or better.\n\nBenson also holds a wide financial edge, having raised about twice as much as James and entering the final weeks with roughly five times his cash on hand. The state's even partisan lean and the lack of an incumbent on the ballot keep the race from being a lock, and third-party candidates appear marginal. James has remained competitive on the debate stage, but the overall evidence points to Benson as the clear favorite.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9339, "margin": 7.39}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9166, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9224, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9193, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8901, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9053, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.911, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9221, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9131, "margin": 6.8}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9322, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.912, "margin": 6.8}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9194, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9194, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.8925, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9071, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9049, "margin": 6.8}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.8998, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.8901, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.8948, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-11